Master Engineering Prompt: "Agent Journey Analytics" Page Integration
1. Objective & Overview
Add a new high-fidelity analytics page/tab titled "Agent Journey Analytics" to our existing enterprise AI banking dashboard prototype.
The goal of this page is to give analytics and AI product teams deep visibility into how banking AI agents (such as Sierra AI) perform in production across 10,000+ customer conversations over a 7-day period.
2. Design System & Styling Guidelines
The new page must seamlessly match the aesthetic, typography, and component styling of our existing dashboard prototype:
 * Background: Clean white (#FFFFFF) with light slate/grey background canvas (#F8FAFC).
 * Borders & Cards: Subtle grey/slate borders (#E2E8F0), rounded corners (rounded-xl), crisp drop shadows (shadow-sm).
 * Color Palette & Accents:
   * Primary Navy: #0F172A (Headers, primary actions, modal tops)
   * Teal/Cyan Accents: #0D9488 / #0EA5E9 (Active selection rings, metrics, navigation highlights)
   * Success Path (Green): #10B981 / #ECFDF5
   * Friction / Drop-off (Amber/Orange): #F59E0B / #FFFBEB
   * Normal Core Processing (Blue): #2563EB / #EFF6FF
   * Intent Drift / Loopback (Purple): #9333EA / #FAF5FF
 * Typography: Inter font family, high contrast, clean scannability, precise numeric hierarchy.
3. Data Architecture: External Mock JSON Fetching
 * Strict Constraint: No hardcoded graph data or metrics inside the HTML/JS frontend code.
 * On page load, the application must fetch data via async/await fetch() from an external file located at /data/agent_journey_mock.json.
 * Why: This mirrors our production architecture, where an automated daily job (e.g., Snowflake / Airflow) exports pre-aggregated conversation telemetry directly to a static cloud storage bucket (AWS S3 / GCS).
 * Filter changes (Date Range, Agent Version, Channel) should simulate re-fetching or filtering this JSON dataset dynamically.
4. Realistic Banking Customer Behaviors (Graph Node Specs)
The graph data must represent messy, non-linear, multi-intent customer behavior rather than a simple 4-box flowchart:
 * Vague Utterance & Disambiguation Loop: Customer says "My card isn't working" \rightarrow Agent triggers a Disambiguation Node (Credit vs. Debit card?) \rightarrow Customer clarifies.
 * Mid-Flow Intent Drift: Customer starts reviewing transactions, suddenly asks "What are your new 30-year home loan interest rates?", receives an FAQ response, and then loops back to resume transaction review or account summary.
 * Verification Friction & Failures: OTP SMS challenge timeouts, identity verification failures, or voice OTP retry paths.
 * Guardrail Interventions & Hallucination Control: Agent attempts an unauthorized fee waiver \rightarrow Guardrail catches it mid-flight \rightarrow Corrects to standard policy answer.
 * Multi-Journey Outcomes:
   * Successful Completion (e.g., Replacement card dispatched).
   * Escalation / Transfer to Human Agent (High-value dispute or complex loan query).
   * Companion App Navigation Drift (Customer directed to mobile app for credit score checks).
   * Abandoned / Unresolved drop-off.
5. UI Layout & Component Architecture
A. Header, Global Filters & KPI Cards
 * Scenario / Agent Switcher: Dropdown supporting 5 distinct journeys (Card Replacement & Fraud Freeze, Account Summary & Intent Drift, Digital KYC Origination, Monthly Statement Snapshots, Dispute Escalation).
 * Global Filter Pills: Date Range (Last 7 Days), Agent Version (v2.4.1-prod), Channel (Omnichannel / App / IVR / WhatsApp).
 * Top KPI Cards:
   * Conversations Started: 10,000
   * Journey Completion Rate: 68.4%
   * Human Handoff Rate: 12.6%
   * Unresolved / Abandoned Rate: 9.8%
B. Central Interactive Journey Map (SVG Canvas)
 * Left-to-right directed graph rendered via SVG Bezier curves (<path d="M... C..." />).
 * Arrow thickness scales proportionally with conversation volume.
 * Curved loopback dashed lines for Intent Drifts and Context Switches.
 * Every node displays: Node Title, Subtitle/Type, Unique Count, and Step Percentage.
 * Interactivity: Clicking any node highlights it on the canvas with a glow border and immediately updates the Right-Side Inspection Drawer.
C. Right-Side Node Inspection Drawer (4-Tab Interface)
When a node is selected, populate the right-hand panel with:
 * Overview Tab: Unique Conversations, Reach Rate %, Median Dwell Time (sec), Execution Error Rate %, and Outgoing Branch Distribution breakdown.
 * Transcripts & Sessions Tab: Searchable list of session IDs passing through that node. Clicking any session opens a modal dialog showing the turn-by-turn chat transcript with expandable tool execution badges (e.g., call_verify_otp(), call_get_transactions(), call_fetch_rates()).
 * Execution Traces Tab: Step-by-step latency waterfall breakdown (Prompt Guardrails \rightarrow Vector Search \rightarrow LLM Inference \rightarrow API Execution) and raw JSON payload viewer.
 * Friction AI Tab: AI-generated root-cause diagnostics explaining why drop-offs or handoffs occurred at that step, with recommended prompt engineering fixes.
